{"id":"pethahiah","name":"Pethahiah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:pethahiah"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Pethahiah","text":"Loosed of the Lord. (1.) The chief of one of the priestly courses (the nineteenth) in the time of David (1 Chr. 24:16). (2.) A Levite (Ezra 10:23). (3.) Neh. 9:5. (4.) A descendant of Judah who had some office at the court of Persia (Neh. 11:24)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6611","lemma":"פְּתַחְיָה","xlit":"Pᵉthachyâh","gloss":"Pethachjah, the name of four Israelites","kjv":"Pethakiah","count":4,"share":1},{"strong":"H3881","lemma":"לֵוִיִּי","xlit":"Lêvîyîy","gloss":"a Levite or descendant of Levi","kjv":"Leviite","count":2,"share":0.5}],"verses":["1Chr.24.16","Ezra.10.23","Neh.9.5","Neh.11.24"],"related":[{"id":"bunni","type":"lexical","strong":"H3881","why":"both lead with לֵוִיִּי (H3881)"},{"id":"hashabiah","type":"lexical","strong":"H3881","why":"both lead with לֵוִיִּי (H3881)"},{"id":"jeshua","type":"lexical","strong":"H3881","why":"both lead with לֵוִיִּי (H3881)"},{"id":"jozabad","type":"lexical","strong":"H3881","why":"both lead with לֵוִיִּי (H3881)"},{"id":"levites","type":"lexical","strong":"H3881","why":"both lead with לֵוִיִּי (H3881)"},{"id":"liberality","type":"lexical","strong":"H3881","why":"both lead with לֵוִיִּי (H3881)"}],"works":[]}
